## Strategy 1: GCP Labels + BigQuery Export

GCP supports **labels** on resources, and you can export billing to BigQuery for analysis.

### Labeling Strategy

```yaml
# Every resource gets these labels
labels:
  customer: "acme-corp"
  environment: "dev"          # dev | stage | uat | prod
  product: "payment-api"
  cost-center: "CUST-001234"
  managed-by: "platform-team"
```

### Apply Labels via Terraform

```hcl
# GKE Namespace with labels (for GKE usage metering)
resource "kubernetes_namespace" "customer_namespace" {
  metadata {
    name = "${var.customer_name}-${var.environment}"
    
    labels = {
      customer    = var.customer_name
      environment = var.environment
      cost-center = var.cost_center
    }
  }
}

# Cloud SQL with labels
resource "google_sql_database_instance" "customer_db" {
  name    = "${var.customer_name}-primary"
  project = "${var.customer_name}-data"
  
  settings {
    user_labels = {
      customer    = var.customer_name
      environment = "all"
      cost-center = var.cost_center
    }
  }
}
```

