## Add to Master Prompt

Here's the section to add to the master prompt under **Architecture Decisions (Locked In)**:

```
11. Cross-Environment Data Sharing (Within Customer):
    - Requirement: A customer's data can be shared between their own environments while remaining isolated from other customers
    - Implementation by storage type:
      
      Cloud SQL:
      - Schema-per-environment: {customer}_{env} (e.g., acme_corp_dev, acme_corp_prod)
      - Shared schema: {customer}_shared for reference data accessible by all environments
      - PostgreSQL users per environment with GRANT-based permissions
      - Non-prod users can SELECT from prod schema (configurable)
      - Prod user can only access prod + shared schemas (strict isolation)
      - Admin user for data cloning operations
      
      BigQuery:
      - Shared tables with tenant_id and environment columns
      - Row-level security policies per service account
      - Non-prod service accounts: Filter on tenant_id only (see all envs)
      - Prod service account: Filter on tenant_id AND environment = 'prod'
      
      GCS:
      - Prefix structure: {customer}/{env}/ and {customer}/shared/
      - IAM conditions on object prefix
      - Non-prod can read all prefixes within customer boundary
      - Prod can only write to prod/, read from shared/
      
    - Data sharing policies (configurable per customer):
      - strict: Each env isolated, only shared resources accessible
      - nonprod-can-read-prod: Non-prod can read all envs, prod isolated (DEFAULT)
      - full-cross-env: All environments can read all others
      
    - Automated data cloning:
      - CronJob clones prod → dev/stage weekly
      - PII anonymization mandatory (email, phone, SSN, addresses)
      - Configurable date filter (last N days)
      - Excludes sensitive tables (audit_logs, etc.)
      
    - Cross-customer isolation:
      - Enforced at infrastructure level (IAM, row-level security)
      - No application-level trust for cross-customer boundaries
      - Service accounts scoped to single customer
      - VPC Service Controls perimeter around data projects
```

