    Infrastructure Composition Engine:
    - Terraform module reads customer product selection
    - For each enabled product, reads product definition
    - Computes union of all required infrastructure
    - Deduplicates shared components (e.g., one Redis if multiple products need it)
    - Applies customer-specific overrides
    - Provisions only what's needed
    
    Composition Logic:
    ```
    For each infrastructure type (Cloud SQL, Redis, BigQuery, etc.):
      needs_{type} = ANY(enabled_products.infrastructure.{type}.required)
      
    If needs_{type}:
      Collect configs from all products requiring this type
      Merge configurations (largest size wins, union of resources)
      Apply customer overrides
      Provision infrastructure
    ```
    
    Day 2 Operations - Adding a Product:
    1. Customer/Operations updates products.yaml (PR)
       - Set enabled: true for new product
       - Configure version and environment settings
    2. PR Validation Pipeline:
       - Validate product exists in catalog
       - Validate version exists
       - Check customer tier allows product
       - Calculate infrastructure delta
       - Estimate cost impact
       - Run Terraform plan
       - Comment on PR with changes summary
    3. PR Approval & Merge
    4. Terraform Apply:
       - Provision new infrastructure components
       - Create service accounts and IAM bindings
       - Set up networking (egress rules, etc.)
    5. ArgoCD Detects Change:
       - ApplicationSet generates new Application
       - Deploys product workload
       - Configures Istio routing
    6. Product Ready for Use
    
    Day 2 Operations - Removing a Product:
    1. Customer/Operations updates products.yaml (PR)
       - Set enabled: false
       - Specify decommissionDate and dataRetentionDays
    2. PR Validation Pipeline:
       - Check no other products depend on this product
       - Validate data retention period specified
       - Require manual approval (platform-admin + customer-success)
    3. PR Approval & Merge
    4. Phased Decommission:
       - Phase 1 (Immediate): Remove application deployment
         - ArgoCD removes workload
         - Revoke service account access
         - Remove Istio routes
       - Phase 2 (After retention period): Archive data
         - Export data to archive bucket
         - Remove infrastructure components
       - Phase 3 (After archive period): Delete data
         - Lifecycle policy deletes archived data
         - Audit logs retained per compliance
    
    Day 2 Operations - Upgrading a Product:
    1. Update version in products.yaml
    2. PR Validation:
       - Check version compatibility
       - Check for breaking changes
       - Validate infrastructure changes (if any)
    3. Apply via ArgoCD:
       - Canary deployment for version change
       - Automated rollback on failure
    4. Infrastructure updates (if needed):
       - Terraform applies infrastructure changes
       - Database migrations handled by product
    
    Infrastructure Dependency Management:
    - Products can declare dependencies on other products
    - Required dependencies: Must be enabled before this product
    - Optional dependencies: Enhanced functionality if enabled
    - Validation prevents removing products that others depend on
    
    Shared vs Dedicated Infrastructure:
    - By default, infrastructure is per-product per-customer
    - Shared option available for some components:
      - Shared Redis: Multiple products share one instance
      - Shared Pub/Sub: Common topics for event-driven integration
    - Configured in customer products.yaml:
      ```yaml
      sharedInfrastructure:
        redis:
          shared: true
          products: [product-a, product-b]
      ```
    
    Cost Management:
    - Each product definition includes cost metadata
    - PR validation shows cost impact of product changes
    - Per-product cost tracking via labels
    - Budget alerts can be set per product
    - Cost estimation formula:
      ```
      Customer Monthly Cost = 
        Σ (Product Base Cost[env] + (Active Users × Per User Cost))
        + Infrastructure Overrides Cost
        + Platform Fee[tier]
      ```
    
